// Ch7 B10 "Leaving Tamsule" (docs/kb/story/beats/act1_ch07.md §2 B10). T08, 15:40, from the coastal
// trader's stern as the party boards for Corrow, looking back at Tamsule and the Bell. A roar comes
// down from the Bell, and a boatman casting off beside them says, to nobody in particular, the ONLY
// mention of the cup's winner in the game (ADR 0020 (h): "mentioned once in passing"). Nobody in the
// party reacts. Rhen, at the stern, looks east, where Tavi's boat went. If he blessed the moorings,
// the camera also finds them under the Bell as they pull away: the rings, and on Oruvel's last ring,
// Pio's side-band, tied (T09, a proposal; otherwise the band is still on his arm). No line. It ends on
// black: Ch8 begins at sea (until ch08/corrow is built, the chapter flow hands off to the end card).
title: ch07_leaving_tamsule
location: ch07/tamsule
---
@letterbox on
@camera T08
@music tidecup_after fade=2.0
@mark rhen rhen_stern walk
@sfx bell_crowd_roar
@wait 1.5
Boatman [neutral]: That'll be Tamsule's cup, then. #line:ch07_leave_001
@wait 1.5
@anim rhen look_at east_water
@wait 2.0
<<if $ch07_blessed_moorings>>
    @camera T09
    @wait 3.0
<<endif>>
@wait 1.0
@fade out 2.0
===
